1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
High above the curving Vltava River, Prague began in the 9th century when Prince Bořivoj laid the stone ramparts of Prague Castle.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
By the 14th century, Holy Roman Emperor Charles IV transformed Prague into the imperial jewel of Central Europe.

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:24,500
Master mason Peter Parler erected the soaring sandstone arches of the Charles Bridge, spanning over 500 meters across the river.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Within the castle walls, St. Vitus Cathedral rose with daring Gothic rib vaults, safeguarding the sacred Bohemian Crown Jewels.

5
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:41,500
During the Renaissance, Emperor Rudolf II welcomed alchemists and astronomers Johannes Kepler and Tycho Brahe to study the heavens.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Thirty expressive Baroque statues of saints were carved along the parapets of the bridge, while golden spires multiplied across the hills.

7
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:59,500
Completed across six centuries and inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage site, Prague endures as the immortal City of a Hundred Spires.
